            <li>No input fields for "Monthly Bill" or "Roof Area" are visible.</li>
            <li>No range sliders are visible.</li>
            <li>No dynamic number outputs (Savings, ROI, Panel Count) are visible.</li>
            <li>The screenshot captures the wrong section of the page entirely if the goal was to review the calculator.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. Typography & Spacing -->
    <div class="section-box">
        <h2>4. Typography and Spacing Problems</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Font Family:</strong> The fonts appear to be system defaults (San Francisco/Inter-like), but without specific inspection, it's hard to confirm if it's strictly "Plus Jakarta Sans" for headings as requested. It looks clean but generic.</li>
            <li><strong>Hierarchy:</strong> The Portfolio Heading ("Rumah Nyata...") is large and bold, which is good, but the subtext is quite light gray, potentially failing contrast checks for some users.</li>
            <li><strong>Card Layout:</strong> The cards themselves have decent internal spacing, but the lack of images makes them look like wireframes rather than a premium finished product.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. Design Feel -->
    <div class="section-box">
        <h2>5. Design Feel: Premium & Residential?</h2>
        <p><strong>Verdict: No.</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Premium?</strong> No. The missing images make it look broken or unfinished. The lack of color (Gold/Green) makes it feel corporate and cold, not warm/premium.</li>
            <li><strong>Residential?</strong> The copy mentions "Rumah" (Home) and "Keluarga" (Family), so the *content* targets residents, but the visual presentation is sterile.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. Layout Breakage -->
